{"id":"612feaedbbff668a64b498ada5bcc79709b23433","axis":"silent","repo":"QwikDev/qwik","sha":"612feaedbbff668a64b498ada5bcc79709b23433","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/error-responses-no-store.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+'@qwik.dev/router': patch","+---","+","+fix: error responses from middleware and route loaders are no longer cached."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/docs/src/routes/docs/(qwikrouter)/route-loader/index.mdx","lines":["@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@ Loader responses come from per-loader JSON endpoints, and the browser HTTP cache"," "," ### `cacheControl`"," ","-Sets the `Cache-Control` header on the loader's JSON responses. It accepts everything the [`cacheControl()`](/docs/(qwikrouter)/caching/index.mdx) request method accepts — `'immutable'`, a max-age number in seconds, an options object — or a function of the request event (return `null` to skip the header). A `Cache-Control` header set inside the loader function wins over the option.","+Sets the `Cache-Control` header on the loader's JSON responses. It accepts everything the [`cacheControl()`](/docs/(qwikrouter)/caching/index.mdx) request method accepts — `'immutable'`, a max-age number in seconds, an options object — or a function of the request event (return `null` to skip the header). A `Cache-Control` header set inside the loader function wins over the option. A failed loader is always sent with `no-store`, so no cache ever reuses the failure."," "," The default is `no-cache`: the browser always revalidates, which pairs well with `eTag` for cheap 304 responses."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/qwik-router/src/middleware/request-handler/handlers/json-request-wrapper.ts","lines":["@@ -58,6 +58,7 @@ export function jsonRequestWrapper(): RequestHandler {","           await sendActionResponse(requestEv, { redirect: location });","         }","       } else if (err instanceof ServerError) {","+        requestEv.headers